message.content:
This is a Caleffi Discal Dirtmag, an air and dirt separator for hydronic systems. It filters or purifies liquids, which points to heading 8421 (filtering or purifying machinery for liquids). Subheading 8421.21 covers water filtering or purifying machinery, and 8421.29 covers other liquid filtering or purifying machinery. Because the fluid may be water or glycol, 8421.29 is likely. Within it, 8421.29.00 splits into 8421.29.0065 ("Other") and others. CBP rulings on air/dirt separators have classified them under 8421.29.0065 as other filtering or purifying machinery for liquids.

The air separator removes gas from liquid, and the magnetic dirt separator removes solids, so it works as a filtering or purifying device. I'm going with 8421.29.0065 from memory of how similar rulings came out, and I have not checked it against the current schedule.

{"hts_code": "8421.29.0065", "reason": "A magnetic air and dirt separator for closed-loop hydronic fluids is filtering or purifying machinery for liquids, falling in the other liquid filtering/purifying machinery provision of heading 8421."}
